# The Flentrop of 1958, Adolphus Busch Hall: a stop
# for dacvoice (voices/README.md, "Stops"). The division's lines (n,
# frame, envelope, chiff) are the same in each of its stops, so they mix.
name Terts 1 3/5
family Hoofdwerk
n 10
frame 8
start 18 dB
attack 0.012 s
peak 0 dB
decay 0 dB/s
sustain 0 dB
release 0.05 s
chiff 0.012 s 16 dB 2 16
# Hoofdwerk: a flute mutation, the note's fifth harmonic.
# An odd harmonic cannot break back: the rank keeps its own pitch to half the
# sample rate (nyquist), alone in zone 5, cut for B6. At C#7 it would sound
# 11,087 Hz, past half the rate, so it has no zone 6.
harmonics 1 1.0  2 0.15  3 0.06  4 0.02
rank 5 1.0 nyquist
zones 6
level 6 dB
# The voicing (voices/README.md, "The voicing"): the speech by the pipe's
# size, and Busch Hall, where the organ stands.
rise 10
room busch
# The celeste: a second read of the table at half the rate, 2 cents
# sharp, a rank a little off the unison.
celeste 2
